// `emit_collect.vl` — the emitter's collection passes: the pre-lowering walks that fill
// the shared emitter tables (`emit_state.vl`) before any bytes are emitted. Function and
// global gathering with lambda lifting (`collectFns`), closure signatures, per-function
// locals and scratch-slot scans, the shape, union and ref-list table builds (`collectA`,
// `collectS`, `collectU`), return-kind inference (`fnRetColsFromRecorded`), and heap-type
// index assignment (`mAssignTypeIndices`). Consults `emit_classify.vl`; writes no bytes.
//
// Additive gating runs through every pass here, and `emit_state.vl`'s header states the
// convention once: a table slot or heap type is interned only when the program uses the
// feature, so a program that does not use it emits the bytes it would emit without the
// feature at all. Each pass below states only its own gate.

